      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-225231",
      ":question/problem": "Given that we are considering only Boolean functions with $3$ variables $x_{1}$, $x_{2}$, and $x_{3}$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $x_{2}^(\u2015)$ is a literal\n2. $x_{1}^(\u2015)\u2227x_{2}$ is a minterm\n3. $(x_{1}\u2227x_{2}^(\u2015))\u2228(x_{1}\u2227x_{2}\u2227x_{3})$ is a disjunctive normal form\n4. $(x_{1}\u2227x_{2}^(\u2015))\u2228(x_{1}\u2227x_{2}\u2227x_{3})$ is a principal disjunctive normal form"
